[HOLE 3] D2D RX lane-bundle skew — set_data_check, and the Genus handoff that
         makes it impossible to land in constraints.sdc

WHAT THIS DOES
    NEW  ASIC/genus-innovus/inputs/pnr_extra_constraints.sdc
         16 set_data_check commands (8 lanes x setup+hold) at +/-0.5 ns.
    EDIT ASIC/genus-innovus/scripts/nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads.mmmc
         adds that file as a SECOND -sdc_files entry, after _syn.sdc.

    No other file changes. No clock created or removed. No clock-to-clock
    exception. Nothing Genus sees changes at all — synthesis is bit-identical.

WHY THE NEW FILE — THIS IS THE FINDING, NOT THE PLUMBING
    The obvious patch is two lines in tidelink_constraints.sdc. It would be
    DEAD ON ARRIVAL, and the tool says so in as many words. Genus 21.1 SDC
    Command Reference, set_data_check, "Current Limitations":

      "Genus does not support data-to-data checks on top-level ports. Genus
       will not infer a check and this will also not be captured as part of
       write_sdc."

    TL_CLK_RX and TL_RX[*] are top-level ports of nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads.
    Innovus reads exactly one SDC — ../outputs/<block>_syn.sdc, the file
    write_sdc produced (mmmc:233-235, 1b_synthesis_eval.tcl:683) — so a
    set_data_check placed in constraints.sdc is dropped at the Genus->Innovus
    handoff and never reaches CTS, placement or timing. It would have read as
    landed in every review and constrained nothing: the same shape as the
    16,653 untimed flops GATE A was built to catch.

    The two obvious escapes are closed by the same reference: "Genus does not
    support data-to-data checks specified on pins belonging to different
    instances" and "Genus also does not support specifying set_data_check
    -from/-to instances". The related pin (clock) and constrained pins (lanes)
    are in different instances by construction. There is no internal form.

    GATE A already prescribes this exact remedy for this exact situation
    (1b_synthesis_eval.tcl:698-700): "If this fires, do NOT hand-edit the
    written SDC - add a second -sdc_files entry to the mmmc."

WHAT IT BOUNDS
    set_input_delay bounds each lane against the forwarded clock independently;
    a per-lane pad->capture cap bounds each lane's absolute delay. Neither
    bounds LANE AGAINST LANE. All eight lanes can sit inside their own windows
    with lane 0 and lane 7 a full skew apart — and cross-lane skew is precisely
    what the deskew FIFO exists to correct, i.e. the quantity whose runtime
    excursions are the marginal-eye failure mode. TideLink's block SDC calls
    this "THE key fix per Part B §3.3 — it bounds the lane-to-lane variance
    that *is* the determinism defect".

THE VALUE: 0.5 ns
    = T_UI/20 at T_UI = 10.0 ns.
    Block SDC:75  RX_BUS_SKEW_NS = T_UI_NS/20.
    Block SDC:66-70 records where the RATIO came from: "the same ratios
    validated on FPGA at T_UI=40 ns (set_max_delay 8 ns ~ T_UI/5, set_bus_skew
    2 ns ~ T_UI/20) scaled down to ASIC T_UI".
    Chain: FPGA-validated 2 ns at 40 ns UI -> ratio 1/20 -> 0.5 ns at 10 ns UI.
    A BUDGET the post-route report must come in under, not a measured value.

MULTIPLICITY — THE RESTRICTION IS ON THE OTHER SIDE
    The block SDC warns that fc_shell's set_data_check -to takes a single pin.
    Cadence restricts the OPPOSITE side. Innovus 21.11 TCR: "Note: You cannot
    use the -from parameter to specify multiple objects." Genus 21.1, same
    sentence. Neither carries it on -to. So a bus on -to is probably legal here
    and no foreach_in_collection is needed for Cadence — but the file loops
    per-lane anyway (16 commands, not 2) so the form sits inside the strictest
    reading of all three tools and survives being ported in any direction.

APPLIES TO
    ASIC/genus-innovus/scripts/nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads.mmmc
    sha256 4ea0bb59b14807eb36d1ea4831e0ef3f03a44920416fe8c6b9cd79796970febb
    plus one new file under ASIC/genus-innovus/inputs/.
    Touches NEITHER constraints.sdc NOR tidelink_constraints.sdc, so it is
    independent of hole1 and hole2 and can be applied in any order.

APPLY
    git apply ASIC/genus-innovus/inputs/patches/hole3-rx-lane-bundle-skew.patch

NOT VALIDATED — AND ONE THING IS GENUINELY UNSETTLED
    No EDA run was made. The documentation settles WHERE the command has to
    live and WHAT multiplicity is legal. It does NOT settle whether a
    set_data_check whose -from is a CLOCK port infers a check at all: the tool
    needs a data arrival event on the related pin, and Innovus's own example
    uses two data signals, not a clock. The block SDC uses the clock-port form
    and calls it the key fix, so the expectation is that it works. Expectation
    is not measurement.

THE FALSIFIABLE CHECK — RUN IT BEFORE CALLING LANE SKEW CONSTRAINED
        report_analysis_coverage -check_type data_check
        report_timing -check_type data_check -from [get_ports TL_CLK_RX] \
                      -to [get_ports {TL_RX[0]}]
    16 data-check arcs (8 setup + 8 hold) must appear. ZERO arcs is a NULL
    RESULT, not a pass, and must never be reported as "lane skew is clean".
    If it infers nothing, move -from to uPAD_TL_CLK_RX/C and the lane side to
    uPAD_TL_RX_<n>/C (PDDW16DGZ_G, gate.v:584684/584688) — those pins carry a
    propagated core arrival that a bare input port may not. Do NOT respond by
    widening 0.5 ns.

    Second check, cheap and independent: the file prints
    "PNR-EXTRA-SDC: D2D RX lane-bundle skew - 8 lanes at +/-0.5 ns" when read.
    No such line in the Innovus log means the mmmc entry did not take.

diff --git a/ASIC/genus-innovus/inputs/pnr_extra_constraints.sdc b/ASIC/genus-innovus/inputs/pnr_extra_constraints.sdc
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ASIC/genus-innovus/inputs/pnr_extra_constraints.sdc
@@ -0,0 +1,142 @@
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# pnr_extra_constraints.sdc — constraints that must reach Innovus DIRECTLY
+#
+# READ THIS FIRST, BECAUSE THE EXISTENCE OF THIS FILE IS THE POINT.
+#
+# Every other SDC in ../inputs is read by GENUS. Innovus never sees them: the
+# mmmc names exactly one constraint file, ../outputs/<block>_syn.sdc, which is
+# what `write_sdc` produced (1b_synthesis_eval.tcl:683). That is the trap
+# design.mk:285-289 and GATE A (1b_synthesis_eval.tcl:685-733) exist to catch --
+# "a clock that binds during elaboration but does not appear HERE reaches
+# neither CTS nor timing, and the run still completes and reports success".
+#
+# THIS FILE IS FOR CONSTRAINTS GENUS CANNOT CARRY ACROSS THAT HANDOFF AT ALL.
+# Not "constraints Genus ignores" -- Genus ignores plenty and still writes them
+# out. These are constraints Genus is DOCUMENTED to drop from write_sdc, so no
+# amount of adding them to constraints.sdc will ever put them in front of
+# Innovus. GATE A's own comment prescribes exactly this remedy: "If this fires,
+# do NOT hand-edit the written SDC - add a second -sdc_files entry to the mmmc."
+#
+# Read AFTER <block>_syn.sdc (mmmc list order), so every clock and port this
+# file references already exists.
+#
+# DO NOT put ordinary constraints here. Anything Genus can carry belongs in
+# ../inputs/constraints.sdc and its four sourced siblings, where synthesis also
+# gets to see it. A constraint that P&R honours and synthesis never saw is a
+# netlist built to the wrong target.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+# ===========================================================================
+# [HOLE 3] D2D RX LANE-BUNDLE SKEW — set_data_check
+# ===========================================================================
+# TideLink's block SDC calls this "THE key fix" for the determinism defect
+# (tidelink/syn/asic/fusion-compiler/inputs/constraints.sdc:181-190) and it has
+# never existed at chiplet top: `grep -r "set_data_check\|set_bus_skew"` over
+# ASIC/genus-innovus/inputs and ASIC/eth-chiplet returns nothing.
+#
+# WHAT IT BOUNDS, AND WHY THE OTHER CONSTRAINTS DO NOT. set_input_delay bounds
+# each lane against the forwarded clock INDEPENDENTLY; a per-lane pad->capture
+# cap bounds each lane's absolute delay. Neither bounds LANE AGAINST LANE. An
+# 8-lane bundle in which every lane individually sits inside its window can
+# still have lane 0 and lane 7 a full skew apart, and cross-lane skew is exactly
+# the quantity the deskew FIFO exists to correct -- i.e. the quantity whose
+# runtime excursions are the marginal-eye failure mode. set_data_check is a
+# RELATIVE (clock-vs-data) constraint with no absolute-window component, so it
+# cannot trigger per-endpoint hold-buffer insertion the way a tightened
+# input-delay window can.
+#
+# THE VALUE: 0.5 ns = T_UI/20, T_UI = 10.0 ns.
+#   block SDC:75  set RX_BUS_SKEW_NS [expr {$T_UI_NS / 20.0}]
+#   block SDC:66-70 records where the RATIO came from: "the same ratios
+#   validated on FPGA at T_UI=40 ns (set_max_delay 8 ns ~ T_UI/5, set_bus_skew
+#   2 ns ~ T_UI/20) scaled down to ASIC T_UI". So the chain is
+#   FPGA-validated 2 ns at 40 ns UI -> ratio 1/20 -> 0.5 ns at this die's 10 ns
+#   UI. It is a BUDGET the post-route report must come in under, not a measured
+#   value; revisit when the package and channel models exist.
+
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# WHY THIS COMMAND CANNOT LIVE IN ../inputs/constraints.sdc. NOT A STYLE CHOICE.
+#
+# Genus 21.1 SDC Command Reference, set_data_check, "Current Limitations":
+#
+#   "Genus does not support data-to-data checks on top-level ports. Genus will
+#    not infer a check and this will also not be captured as part of write_sdc."
+#
+# TL_CLK_RX and TL_RX[*] are top-level ports of nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads, so a
+# set_data_check written in constraints.sdc would be dropped from
+# <block>_syn.sdc and Innovus would never see it -- a constraint that reads as
+# landed and constrains nothing, in a file whose whole history is that failure.
+#
+# The same reference closes the two obvious escapes: "Genus does not support
+# data-to-data checks specified on pins belonging to different instances" and
+# "Genus also does not support specifying set_data_check -from/-to instances".
+# The related pin (the clock) and the constrained pins (the lanes) are in
+# different instances by construction. There is no internal form either.
+# Innovus is the only place this can be expressed. Hence this file.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# PER-PORT, NOT A BUS ON -to. Both references restrict multiplicity, and they
+# restrict DIFFERENT SIDES from the one the block SDC's comment warns about:
+#
+#   Innovus 21.11 TCR, set_data_check, -from:
+#     "Note: You cannot use the -from parameter to specify multiple objects."
+#   Genus 21.1, set_data_check, -from:
+#     "You cannot use the -from parameter to specify multiple objects."
+#
+# Neither carries that sentence on -to (both say only "use only one -to
+# parameter per command"), so a bus on -to is probably legal in Cadence -- the
+# fc_shell restriction the block SDC works around is the mirror image. `-from`
+# here is a single port either way. The loop below spends 16 commands instead
+# of 2 to sit inside the STRICTEST reading of both tools plus fc_shell, so this
+# form survives being ported in any direction. That is worth 14 lines of log.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+set _bs_skew 0.5
+
+if {[llength [get_ports -quiet TL_CLK_RX]] != 1} {
+    error "pnr_extra_constraints.sdc: TL_CLK_RX did not bind. The RX lane-bundle\
+ skew check would be silently absent -- the exact class of defect this file was\
+ created to avoid. Refusing to continue."
+}
+set _bs_n 0
+foreach _l {0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7} {
+    set _p [get_ports -quiet "TL_RX\[$_l\]"]
+    if {[llength $_p] != 1} {
+        error "pnr_extra_constraints.sdc: TL_RX\[$_l\] did not bind. Refusing to\
+ continue -- a partially-applied bundle skew check is worse than none, because\
+ the report looks populated."
+    }
+    set_data_check -from [get_ports TL_CLK_RX] -to $_p -setup $_bs_skew
+    set_data_check -from [get_ports TL_CLK_RX] -to $_p -hold  $_bs_skew
+    incr _bs_n
+}
+if {$_bs_n != 8} {
+    error "pnr_extra_constraints.sdc: applied $_bs_n/8 lane skew checks."
+}
+puts "PNR-EXTRA-SDC: D2D RX lane-bundle skew - $_bs_n lanes at +/-$_bs_skew ns\
+ (T_UI/20, T_UI = 10.0 ns)"
+unset _bs_skew _bs_n _l _p
+
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# VERIFY IT INFERRED, DO NOT ASSUME IT DID. The one thing this file cannot
+# settle from documentation is whether a set_data_check whose -from is a CLOCK
+# port produces a check at all: the tool needs a DATA arrival event at the
+# related pin, and Innovus's own example uses two data signals (XE/SE), not a
+# clock. The block SDC uses the clock-port form and calls it the key fix, so the
+# expectation is that it works -- but "expected" is not "measured".
+#
+# THE FALSIFIABLE CHECK, post-CTS or later:
+#     report_analysis_coverage -check_type data_check
+#     report_timing -check_type data_check -from [get_ports TL_CLK_RX] \
+#                   -to [get_ports {TL_RX[0]}]
+# 16 data-check arcs (8 setup + 8 hold) must appear. ZERO arcs means the check
+# inferred nothing -- that is a NULL RESULT, not a pass, and it must not be
+# reported as "lane skew is clean".
+#
+# IF IT INFERS NOTHING, the next thing to try is anchoring -from at the RX clock
+# pad's core-side output pin rather than the port -- uPAD_TL_CLK_RX/C, a
+# PDDW16DGZ_G in the shipping netlist (gate.v:584684), with the lane side moved
+# to the matching uPAD_TL_RX_<n>/C. That pin carries a propagated arrival in the
+# core, which a bare input port may not. Do NOT respond by widening 0.5 ns.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
--- a/ASIC/genus-innovus/scripts/nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads.mmmc
+++ b/ASIC/genus-innovus/scripts/nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads.mmmc
@@ -230,9 +230,37 @@
    -late_timing_condition {tc_typ}\
    -rc_corner default_rc_corner_typical
 
+# SECOND -sdc_files ENTRY, ADDED 2026-08-18. NOT a convenience.
+#
+# Genus is DOCUMENTED to drop some constraints from write_sdc entirely -- its
+# SDC Command Reference says of set_data_check: "Genus does not support
+# data-to-data checks on top-level ports. Genus will not infer a check and this
+# will also not be captured as part of write_sdc." So the D2D RX lane-bundle
+# skew check can never arrive here through <block>_syn.sdc no matter what
+# ../inputs/constraints.sdc contains.
+#
+# This is the remedy GATE A already prescribes for exactly this situation
+# (1b_synthesis_eval.tcl:698-700): "If this fires, do NOT hand-edit the written
+# SDC - add a second -sdc_files entry to the mmmc."
+#
+# ORDER MATTERS AND IS NOT ALPHABETICAL. _syn.sdc is FIRST because it creates
+# every clock; the overlay only references them. Innovus reads the list in
+# order and get_clocks cannot name a clock that does not exist yet -- the same
+# reasoning design.mk:270-277 gives for why SDC_FILES is a single explicit
+# entry rather than a sorted glob.
+#
+# ${design_home} rather than the ../inputs relative form used elsewhere in the
+# repo: this file is loaded by read_mmmc, whose working directory is a property
+# of the Cadence command, and design_home is resolved from $::env at the top of
+# this file precisely so it is valid in every Tcl context.
+#
+# ANYTHING GENUS CAN CARRY BELONGS IN ../inputs/constraints.sdc INSTEAD. A
+# constraint P&R honours and synthesis never saw means a netlist built to the
+# wrong target.
 create_constraint_mode -name default_constraint_mode\
    -sdc_files\
-    [list ../outputs/nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads_syn.sdc]
+    [list ../outputs/nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads_syn.sdc \
+          ${design_home}/ASIC/genus-innovus/inputs/pnr_extra_constraints.sdc]
 
 create_analysis_view -name default_analysis_view_setup -constraint_mode default_constraint_mode -delay_corner default_delay_corner_max
 create_analysis_view -name default_analysis_view_hold -constraint_mode default_constraint_mode -delay_corner default_delay_corner_min
